==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Baa Baa]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 2~20 seconds<sup>60f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Gory|Gories]] spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 3~40 seconds<sup>90f~1,200f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Squire Rel]] (100%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.27~1.33 seconds<sup>8f~40f</sup>.
**4 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 2~6.67 seconds<sup>60f~200f</sup>.
**4 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 6.67~12 seconds<sup>200f~360f</sup>.
**1 [[Le'boin]] spawns.
**12 [[Squire Rel]]s (40,000%) spawn, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Not too difficult. [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk Cat]], [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]] and a strong, spammable [[:Category:Area Attack Cats|Area Attacker]] like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris]] will clear this stage quite easily. The overbuffed Squire Rels might sound intimidating, but their health and range aren't too high, allowing stacks of DPS units to quickly cut through then before they do too much damage.

